Sabriel was one of Sophie's first Titans and has since become her favorite to use in battle against [[the Organization]].{{source|Huntik.com/Profiles|Huntik.com}}

Sophie invoked Sabriel from a rooftop in Venice to help [[Dante Vale]] and [[Lok Lambert]] whilst they were being pursued by [[Organization]] [[Suits]]. The pair jumped down and defeated a [[Redcap]]. {{source|The Casterwill Client}} In the [[Prague Huntik Hotel]], Dante scanned Sabriel on the [[Holotome]]. Sabriel was later invoked to fight a Redcap in the house of [[Jodis Lore]] on the [[Road of Alchemists]] and fought against [[DeFoe|DeFoe's]] forces. After Dante obtained the [[Amulet]] of [[Metagolem]], Sabriel regrouped with the rest of the Huntik team. {{source|Words of Truth, Heart of Lies}}

During the final confrontation with [[the Professor]], Sabriel was affected by the Spikes ability of [[Dominator]] and, in protecting Sophie, refused to return to her Amulet and continued to endure further attacks from [[Nordrake]]. She and her Amulet were then destroyed by a [[Rippleburst]] spell from the Professor thanks to Sabriel exhausting her energies using her Supertough ability. After using this ability to protect Sophie, Sabriel disappeared, apparently for good. {{source|The Mission}} The loss of Sabriel deeply affected Sophie long after the Professor's defeat, leaving her feeling weak and ineffective. {{source|Doorway to Huntik}}

Thanks to the power of [[Powerbonding]], however, Sabriel reappeared by Sophie's side with her summoning icon appearing directly on Sophie's hand. Powerbonded Sabriel returned in the [[Crystal Caves]] to save her Seeker from a treacherous situation against [[Undine|Undine, the Water Spirit]] and [[Coralgolem]] in which Sophie was unable to summon any of her other Titans. After the trial, Sabriel was reunited with her sister Titan, [[Sorcerel]]. {{source|Cave of the Casterwills}} Powerbonded Sabriel has since been actively used by Sophie to fight against both the Organization and the [[Blood Spiral]].

When Sabriel became Powerbonded, she transcended the need for a traditional Amulet, which she no longer had, and instead could be invoked from Sophie's hand. Powerbonded Sabriel gained golden armor, a cape, and the capacity to float for a limited time. {{source|Cave of the Casterwills}} Among her new abilities are:
*'''Counterattack''' - swiftly strikes an enemy after fending off their attack. {{source|Gremlow Infestation!}}
*'''Diving Kick''' - an offensive kick made by jumping through the air and launching off her swords. {{source|Back Home}} 
*'''Double Parry''' - a defensive stance by crossing her two swords. {{source|Zhalia's Mission}}
*'''Sunstrike''' - a deflection of incoming offensive spells. {{source|Lok's Leadership}}
*'''Synchronised Attack''' - mimics her Seeker's moves perfectly. {{source|Knight of the Willblade}} 
*'''Truth Shield''' - creates a force field to protect herself and those around her from incoming attacks. {{source|Knight of the Willblade}} 

When used together with Sorcerel and Sophie, they can activate the '''Triple Truth Shield''' ability to protect all three of them and knock back enemy forces. {{source|Lok's Leadership}}
